// Rex login server accounts file for lumquat (embedded HuJSON).
//
// Format: `rex login-server --accounts`. HuJSON (JSON plus comments and
// trailing commas) because Rex parses it with github.com/tailscale/hujson;
// strict `decodeStrict` means the shape matters: only `version`, `accounts`,
// and `defaults` at the top level, and only `principals` inside an account.
//
// This file is written by `environment.etc."rex/accounts.jsonc"` in
// modules/features/rex.nix — the same /etc path Rex reads by default — so it is
// managed like every other /etc file NixOS writes: atomic, generation-pinned,
// and at exactly the mode set there (on a plain file, because
// `environment.etc` silently ignores `mode` for symlinked (source-less) entries).
//
// What it grants today.
//
//   podman   the operator account, by the owner's Tailscale *login*
//   *        any regular account (UID >= 1000) that the caller names —
//            systemd/podman dynamic users come and go, so they cannot be
//            listed statically. Same single principal, so the wildcard adds
//            reach without widening who may act.
//
// The principal is a LOGIN, not a tag. lumquat's own node is tagged
// (`tag:prod`), so it has no login and reports `LoginName: null` — but the node
// is the *server*; the principals here describe the callers. The owner attaches
// as `ashebanow@gmail.com` (verified: `tailscale status --json | .User | .[] |
// select(.DisplayName|test("Andrew"))`), and that is the only principal listed.
//
// Not used deliberately:
//
//   tailscale:tag:*    matches ANY tag on ANY node, and would admit lumquat's
//                      own `tag:prod` node too. The login above is stricter and
//                      is what actually identifies the owner. Replace with
//                      `tailscale:tag:prod` (verified to parse) if a second
//                      tagged machine should ever attach.
//   root               Rex maps UID 0 warily, and nothing here needs root: the
//                      account servers run as the account they serve.
//   anonymous          a valid principal, but it matches nobody while the only
//                      listener is Tailscale Serve — and it would match the
//                      moment a plain TCP listener were added. Never add it
//                      unless the tailnet ACLs are the only door.
//
// `defaults` must name an account that exists. lumquat has no `ashebanow`
// account (`getent passwd ashebanow` — nothing), only `podman`, so podman is
// what a bare https://lumquat.<tailnet>.ts.net lands on.
//
// A principal key is a JSON key string, so a literal wildcard account in
// `defaults` reads awkwardly ("*") but is the same value either way.
{
  "version": 1,
  "accounts": {
    "podman": {
      "principals": [
        "tailscale:ashebanow@gmail.com"
      ]
    },
    "*": {
      "principals": [
        "tailscale:ashebanow@gmail.com"
      ]
    }
  },
  "defaults": {
    "tailscale:ashebanow@gmail.com": "podman"
  }
}
